From 80961f400b7780ce981e6c34335486f12093466b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yihou <yihou@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 09:23:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/25] sglang DSA: converge patches with upstream, bake them
 into the image

Reshapes two of the four patches to follow the upstream PRs that fix the same
bug classes, and adds a build step so the image actually contains them.

Patch changes:

* dsa_indexer_hip_dp_padded_rows -- reshaped to PR #32762's form (NPU, same
  bug class): one boolean gates both the trim and the restore, and the
  post-kernel row count is ASSERTED before the padding is re-attached. The
  previous form re-derived the condition and used `topk_result.shape[0] ==
  q_offset` as a silent guard, so a shape drift would skip the restore and
  hand back a short tensor -- a wrong answer instead of a crash.

* eagle_worker_v2_uniform_draft_graph -> draft_cuda_graph_dp_vote. Same fix,
  PR #32209's placement: the draft-graph vote rides the MLP-sync all-gather
  the scheduler already performs instead of adding a gloo all-reduce per
  draft() call. Zero extra collectives, and it separates the draft vote from
  the generic can_cuda_graph vote. Measured at 97.1% draft-graph usage.

Build:

* Dockerfile.sglang.dmabuf now applies the patch set via
  apply_sglang_dsa_patches.sh, which verifies each patch reached the BYTECODE
  -- a stale __pycache__ entry silently reverts a patch and has already
  invalidated a full experiment here. APPLY_SGLANG_DSA_PATCHES=0 builds stock.
  The base tag stays pinned: patches apply at --fuzz=0, so a base bump fails
  the build instead of mis-applying.

README corrections, all from `gh` this time rather than from notes:

* "this mechanism appears unreported" was false -- #32527 reported it
  independently two days before we fixed it;
* "#32209 all-gathers can_cuda_graph, so its vote would not have fixed it" was
  false -- it adds a separate can_draft_cuda_graph field, the same idea as
  ours, better placed;
* "#32209 is CI red" was never checked; its state is REVIEW_REQUIRED.

Also records a negative result: porting #32209's OTHER half (trim q/top-k
instead of expanding the page table) fails 0/32 across seven runs and three
node pairs, seventeen candidate causes eliminated, root cause not identified.
Our expand form stays until that is understood.

The 2026-07-29 numbers in the README were measured with the v1 shapes; each
reshape was re-validated separately but never together. That is now stated
rather than implied, pending the end-to-end run.

